# The service entry

The service starts here. This is the runtime edge — the one place an Effect program begins — that launches the notes server on its port, under the Design logger, over the Node platform. A developer runs it with `bun serve`, and it runs the same on Node.

The port comes from the environment, and falls back to 5710 when nothing sets it. The Design logger sits beneath the server, so every line the server writes lands in `design.log`, and the Node platform's services supply the filesystem the logger and the store draw on. `Layer.launch` runs the server until the process ends.

The store is the local one — a SQLite file the service names for itself — which is what `NoteStore.layer` now binds, so the entry names no database at all. A service on a laptop should need nothing stood up before it starts.

=>

import { Effect, Layer } from 'effect'
import { NodeRuntime, NodeServices } from '@effect/platform-node'
import { notesServer, designLogger } from './api'

const port = Number(process.env.PORT ?? 5710)

NodeRuntime.runMain(
  Layer.launch(notesServer(port)).pipe(
    Effect.provide(designLogger),
    Effect.provide(NodeServices.layer),
  ),
)

